# KV_TIER_MIN_TOKENS+ tokens is also written to local disk on every rank when it is kept, in blocks of 2,048 tokens
# named by a hash chain over the token ids (a later turn writes only its new blocks), staged through a bounded pinned
# ring between rounds. A request that extends a state the pool no longer holds (evicted, a restart, a crash) reads it
# back in slices between the other streams' rounds. Every file is fsynced before its rename; each block, the ids and
# the small state carry a CRC-32 checked on every read (a failure on any rank drops the state on every rank and the
# request prefills). Folders keyed on the build and the settings the ranks agree on, as the spill tier's. One disk
# tier at a time: a start with --spill-gib as well stops. New tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/kvtier.py, hooks in
# multi.py and the engine's rank check. By BadAd84.
